WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
If you are an employee, your employer deducts income tax and National Insurance from each payslip: this is the PAYE system. Current tax year: 6 April 2026 to 5 April 2027.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The first £12,570 a year is tax-free (the Personal Allowance). From £12,571 to £50,270 you pay 20%; from £50,271 to £125,140, 40%; above that, 45% (the bands are different in Scotland).

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:44.600
Your tax code appears on your payslip. The most common one is 1257L. If you are given an emergency code, you will overpay until it is corrected.

4
00:00:44.600 --> 00:01:00.600
When you change jobs you get a P45; each April, a P60 with what you earned and paid. Keep them. With the HMRC app or your GOV.UK account you can see your tax code and what you have paid.

5
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.600
Say it aloud: “I think my tax code is wrong.”.
